   "reasoning_summary": "C11H11NO2S has DoU 7. The AA'BB' pattern at 7.59/6.84 (1, 2), with carbons 161.0, 128.1, 121.2 and 114.3 (8-11), plus OCH3 at 3.72/55.3 (4, 13), indicates a 4-methoxyphenyl group (4 DoU). That leaves C4H4NOS with 3 DoU. A lone CH at 6.18 with its carbon at 99.9 (3, 12) and two downfield quaternary carbons at 167.7 and 162.6 (6, 7) fit an isoxazole. A methyl at 2.52/15.4 (5, 14) fits SCH3. A 3-aryl-5-(methylthio)isoxazole matches the typical C5-S near 168, C4 near 100 and C3 near 162. The 5-aryl-3-SMe regioisomer is the main alternative. No 1H integrals were supplied, so proton counts are inferred from the formula."
  },
